   "title": "Models and .whl files",
   "properties": {
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.1",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    }
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Required models for Flux.2 D GGUF Workflow:\n\nFlux.2 Dev GGUF Model: https://huggingface.co/city96/FLUX.2-dev-gguf/tree/main\nText Encoder: https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/tree/main/split_files/text_encoders\nVAE: https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/tree/main/split_files/vae\n\nIf you need FP8 FLUX.2 D Version - https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/tree/main/split_files/diffusion_models\nIf you need Text Encoder in GGUF - https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Mistral-Small-3.2-24B-Instruct-2506-GGUF/tree/main\nFile save location\n\nComfyUI/\n├───📂 models/\n│   ├───📂 diffusion_models/\n│   │   ├─── flux2-dev-Q8_0.gguf\n│   ├───📂 loras/\n│   │   ├─── Any loras if you want (only for Flux.2 D, not Flux.1 D)\n│   ├───📂 text_encoders/\n│   │   └─── mistral_3_small_flux2_bf16.safetensors (or fp8 if you have low vram)\n│   └───📂 vae/\n│       └── flux2-vae.safetensors\n\n\nSageAttention.whl - https://github.com/woct0rdho/SageAttention/releases/tag/v2.2.0-windows. To install sageattention, u can .whl change to .zip and:\n1. If u don't have sageattention, just put folders from .zip to ComfyUI\\python_embeded\\Lib\\site-packages\n2. If u have older version sageattention, delete folders with sageattention in ComfyUI\\python_embeded\\Lib\\site-packages and put new folders from .zip\n\nTo install Triton (if u don't have Triton) go to ComfyUI\\python_embeded and install by command [pip install triton] via cmd\n\nif you got error BaseLoaderKJ._patch_modules.<locals>.attention_sage() got an unexpected keyword argument 'transformer_options', use run_nvidia_gpu - sageattention.bat instead run_nvidia_gpu.bat in ComfyUI from .zip archive\n\n\n\n"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "Required models for Flux.2 D GGUF Workflow:\n\nFlux.2 Dev GGUF Model: https://huggingface.co/city96/FLUX.2-dev-gguf/tree/main\nText Encoder: https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/tree/main/split_files/text_encoders\nVAE: https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/tree/main/split_files/vae\n\nIf you need FP8 FLUX.2 D Version - https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/tree/main/split_files/diffusion_models\nIf you need Text Encoder in GGUF - https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Mistral-Small-3.2-24B-Instruct-2506-GGUF/tree/main\nFile save location\n\nComfyUI/\n├───📂 models/\n│   ├───📂 diffusion_models/\n│   │   ├─── flux2-dev-Q8_0.gguf\n│   ├───📂 loras/\n│   │   ├─── Any loras if you want (only for Flux.2 D, not Flux.1 D)\n│   ├───📂 text_encoders/\n│   │   └─── mistral_3_small_flux2_bf16.safetensors (or fp8 if you have low vram)\n│   └───📂 vae/\n│       └── flux2-vae.safetensors\n\n\nSageAttention.whl - https://github.com/woct0rdho/SageAttention/releases/tag/v2.2.0-windows. To install sageattention, u can .whl change to .zip and:\n1. If u don't have sageattention, just put folders from .zip to ComfyUI\\python_embeded\\Lib\\site-packages\n2. If u have older version sageattention, delete folders with sageattention in ComfyUI\\python_embeded\\Lib\\site-packages and put new folders from .zip\n\nTo install Triton (if u don't have Triton) go to ComfyUI\\python_embeded and install by command [pip install triton] via cmd\n\nif you got error BaseLoaderKJ._patch_modules.<locals>.attention_sage() got an unexpected keyword argument 'transformer_options', use run_nvidia_gpu - sageattention.bat instead run_nvidia_gpu.bat in ComfyUI from .zip archive\n\n\n\n"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
